.TH SPAN 1
.SH NAME
span \- bridge builder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/span
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Span
is a bridge builder.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Build a bridge to hold up the red masses, which grow and shrink as the
simulation runs.
Place masses and members (m/c/s/w), then press space to run the simulation.
The lowest cost bridge that stays standing wins.
Keys v and d select move and delete.
The cost and elapsed time are shown at the top of the window, and the run
state and current mode are also on-screen buttons at the top left, which
may be clicked.
.PP
Pressing space to run snapshots the design.
Enter then restarts from that snapshot, so a bridge may be tried, restarted
and tweaked repeatedly.
Ctrl-N discards the snapshot and starts again from the default bridge.
Designs may be written to and read from
.B $home/span
with Ctrl-A and Ctrl-O.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B m
Mass mode
.TP
.B c
Concrete mode
.TP
.B s
Steel mode
.TP
.B w
Wire mode
.TP
.B v
Move mode
.TP
.B d
Delete mode
.TP
.B LMB
Place/edit per mode; press the run or mode button
.TP
.B RMB
Cycle mode
.TP
.B space
Run/stop simulation
.TP
.B Enter
Restart from the design as it was when the run began
.TP
.B Ctrl-N
New bridge, discarding the saved design
.TP
.B Ctrl-O
Open a saved design from
.B $home/span
.TP
.B Ctrl-A
Save the design to
.B $home/span
.TP
.B Esc
Save the design, then exit
.TP
.B q
Exit without saving
.PD
.SH FILES
.TF $home/span
.TP
.B $home/span
saved designs, one file per design
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/span.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR ode (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The TempleOS File and Play pulldown menus are not drawn; every menu action
is on a key or on one of the two on-screen buttons.
Shift-Esc (abort without saving) is
.B q
here, because the keyboard channel does not distinguish it from Esc.
